  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "When I upload my model after the update, my particles appear without their texture under the Shapes tab inside the particle system. Instead of displaying the texture as they should, they appear as if no texture was ever applied.\n\nI noticed that when I uploaded using \"Build & Test Offline,\" the particles appeared correctly. However, when I uploaded normally to VRChat, the texture was removed, and the particles appeared without it.\n\nThis issue only started happening after the latest update (2025.1.1). It was not occurring in previous uploads before the update.\n\nI checked the patch notes for VRChat, but there was no mention of changes related to the particle system, the SDK, or the upload process.\n\nTo help illustrate the issue, I will provide images showing:\n\nWhat my particle system looks like in Unity before uploading.\n\nWhat it looks like after uploading.\n\nA comparison of the affected particle system property.\n\nAn example of how the particles appear in Unity when no texture is applied (which is how they look in-game).\n\nKeep in mind that everything was working fine before the 2025.1.1 update.",
